# iOS acquisition (code, 2026-08-17)

`IOSProvider.acquire` is fail-soft per step; **empty total fails**. Order:

1. Full `idevicebackup2` only if `ios_libimobiledevice_backup_enabled` (default **False**). Not fail-soft if enabled.
2. `acquire_ios_afc_media`: `pull_recent_media.py` DCIM **and** (if `ios_photo_library_recovery_enabled`) `pull_library_artifacts.py` Hidden / Recently Deleted / V2 cache / `.ithmb` / ACHANGE+WAL metadata. Same 3/6-month cutoff as Android for DCIM, hidden, deleted, purge metadata. Cache/ithmb are **not** date-filtered. Commit only verified manifest artifacts (`ios_hidden`, `ios_recently_deleted`, `ios_recovered_cache`, `ios_deleted_metadata`). Library recovery lives **inside** AFC media.
3. AFC docs (`pull_shared_docs.py`) — no time window. Backend sets `UDID` env; the script currently uses usbmux without serial.
4. Selective backup SMS+contacts (`acquire_ios_backup_comms`); `service` distinguishes SMS vs iMessage. SMS/iMessage honor 3/6-month cutoff (unknown dates kept); contacts unbounded in time, QUICK count-capped at 200.
5. `acquire_ios_social_ui`: in-tree WDA IG+X only (`ios_social_targets`). Maps to `visible_ui` using Android package IDs `com.instagram.android` / `com.twitter.android`. Facebook flow exists in the puller (`fb-profile`) but is **not** wired. WDA/social failure must not discard earlier media.

QUICK uses numeric caps (media 40, docs 30, SMS/contacts 200, social shots 2). FULL `0` = uncapped for AFC/docs/messages. Photos library FULL is **bounded** (Field `ge=1`, not 0-uncapped). Social FULL `0` is remapped to **500** (WDA ceiling).

Invoke scripts with the puller `.venv`, session-scoped work dirs under staging, then delete work dirs. No copy from prior session dirs. No `import ios-media-puller`.

WDA IPA: GitHub Actions reads **repo-root** `.github/workflows/build-wda.yml` only (nested `ios-media-puller/.github` is ignored). Artifact `WebDriverAgentRunner-ipa`; unsigned; local AltServer. Prefer `~/wda` (newer of regular vs nodsym). Acquisition sets `IOS_SKIP_WDA_INSTALL=1`. Selectors/limits stay in SIKSIK host code.
